close_reason: "Landed the round-4 review fixes in this vendored scanner and repaired the closure metadata chain-validly. Compound one-line assignments after then/else/elif/do are now recorded by splitting a line on unquoted semicolons before the anchored match, so a variable-routed publish inside a one-line compound is audited instead of invisible behind an attested sibling. Sibling if-branches and case arms no longer share bindings: else/elif and a case arm's ;; pop same-depth bindings, while enclosing-scope bindings survive, each direction covered by its own test. pm-todos-9clr's closure metadata now follows its final fix history via a chain-valid reopen and re-close, after measuring that hand-reordering the hash-chained history broke pm health's history-drift gate (exit 1, chain and hash mismatch). All three regression tests verified red with their fix reverted; 254/254 pass; coverage thresholds met; pm health --strict-exit exits 0; changelog regenerated and checked."
body: ""
